this month we are celebrating the 32nd  anniversary of the americans with  disabilities act but with the lifting of  covert precautions many people with  disabilities as well as those facing  serious illness feel forgotten about 7  million americans have compromised  immune systems which puts them at a  higher risk for severe covet and  possibly even death earlier this year  the cdc director said that among  vaccinated people it's mostly those with  comorbidities who are dying from the  virus but many in the disability  community were outraged by that  statement feeling it devalued their  lives  they began sharing their stories using  the hashtag my disabled life is worthy  we spoke with three people with  disabilities about their experiences  we've faced mass death  in the disabled community as a result of  kovid  my name is ola o.j woomy  and i'm a disability rights activist in  the washington dc metropolitan area  since i was 9 years old i have been  disabled i was diagnosed with a rare  heart condition i needed to be put on  the organ transplant waiting list for a  heart and kidney a few years after my  transplants i was diagnosed with a rare  form of post-transplant cancer  as a disabled person getting covered  could be a death sentence this is  something that i take every night i live  with chronic migraine which means that i  get 15 or more migraine attacks a month  i'm currently living at a migraine every  single day my condition is an invisible  disability because you can't see it but  that's the thing that disabled doesn't  have a look anyone can be disabled here  we go my name is carm rose fialo my  pronouns are she her i'm a queer  disabled latina and i am a disability  advocate to the pandemic with mask  mandates being lifted in nearly every  state  the mass mandates had been lifted on  airplanes and i didn't realize like how  soon it was effective and i was flying  home the next day and i got on  an airplane and i was shocked by how  many people weren't wearing masks i'm  already disabled and even though i'm  vaccinated and boosted and more likely  to get mild covered i still have an  equal chance of getting long covet and  for me to add chronic fatigue and all  those symptoms on top of what i'm  already dealing with it would just be  extremely detrimental and debilitating i  think it's hard to process  what's actually happening right now  which is  most people are going to get covered the  way that that falls on my ears is  that  we  should just expect  that  we might get severely ill and die  that it's inevitable  my name is christine mitchell and i have  marfan syndrome which is a connective  tissue disorder my anxiety around  contracting covid is that i am at high  risk if i got it even when i've had the  flu it has impacted me  pretty severely the overwhelming number  of deaths over 75 percent occurred in  people who had at least four  comorbidities so really these are people  who were unwell to begin with to hear  that  that  the death of someone like me was  considered encouraging  news  i think was also very painful the way to  make people with disabilities not feel  excluded is to give them positions of  power i would like to see actual people  with disabilities actual doctors and  professionals with disabilities leading  the cdc's effort it's time for america  to get back to work and fill our great  downtowns again with people people  working from home can feel safe and  begin to return to their offices  i definitely feel  like disabled and immunocompromised  people are being forgotten  as we  do this return to normal people should  have the choice and the flexibility to  work from home and  i understand and can appreciate that you  know working in person working with your  team is really beneficial but i think  that we just need to be flexible with  people and give people the choice i  think  at an individual level  things like  mask mandates things like vaccination  things like  access to testing  remain very important  the thing about being disabled  is that people feel that it can never  happen to them  but kovit has proven  that it can make you disabled it is a  mass disabling event that has created  disabilities for thousands of people  you can prevent yourself  and others from becoming disabled by  simply wearing a mask
 

